From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 20:16:53 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] phy: qcom: qmp-combo: Clamp the USB4 outputs in the noirq
 phase of system sleep

The USB4 outputs are clamped across system suspend for a host router
that is kept, after the router's MCU is halted and until before it is
started again. The router is now halted and started in the noirq
phase, so the clamp moves there with it. The order against the router
stays what it was, in either phase: the router is a consumer of the
PHY.

Assisted-by: Claude Fable 5.2
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c | 11 ++++++-----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
index 19522682b..758d609a2 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
@@ -5237,10 +5237,11 @@ static int __maybe_unused qmp_combo_runtime_resume(struct device *dev)
 /*
  * A USB4 router kept across system suspend leaves the PHY initialized and
  * powered while its MCU is halted. Clamp the USB4 outputs meanwhile, as
- * autonomous mode does; the router's callbacks run before ours on suspend
- * and after ours on resume.
+ * autonomous mode does. The router is halted and started again in the noirq
+ * phase, so that is where this is done; the router's callbacks run before
+ * ours on suspend and after ours on resume.
  */
-static int __maybe_unused qmp_combo_suspend(struct device *dev)
+static int __maybe_unused qmp_combo_suspend_noirq(struct device *dev)
 {
 	struct qmp_combo *qmp = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 
@@ -5252,7 +5253,7 @@ static int __maybe_unused qmp_combo_suspend(struct device *dev)
 	return 0;
 }
 
-static int __maybe_unused qmp_combo_resume(struct device *dev)
+static int __maybe_unused qmp_combo_resume_noirq(struct device *dev)
 {
 	struct qmp_combo *qmp = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 
@@ -5265,7 +5266,7 @@ static int __maybe_unused qmp_combo_resume(struct device *dev)
 }
 
 static const struct dev_pm_ops qmp_combo_pm_ops = {
-	SET_SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(qmp_combo_suspend, qmp_combo_resume)
+	SET_NOIRQ_SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(qmp_combo_suspend_noirq, qmp_combo_resume_noirq)
 	SET_RUNTIME_PM_OPS(qmp_combo_runtime_suspend,
 			   qmp_combo_runtime_resume, NULL)
 };
